<title>ITALY: Italy to cut deficit to 3% of GDP.</title>
<headline>Italy to cut deficit to 3% of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy looks set to cut its deficit to three percent of gross domestic product (GDP) in 1997, meeting a key requirement for countries wishing to join the single European currency, Finance Minister Vincenzo Visco said.</p>
<p>A Treasury source added that state accounts from the first six months of the year were in line with a government target for a full year deficit/GDP ratio of 3.0 percent.</p>
<p>Italy's deficit/GDP ratio in 1996 was 6.7 percent.</p>
</text>
